#
# Knock Nation Bag — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and paste your values. .env.local is gitignored;
# this example file is committed and must never contain real credentials.
#
#   cp .env.local.example .env.local
#
# Find all three values in the Supabase dashboard:
#   Project Settings -> API
#
# Restart the dev server after editing — Next.js reads env files at boot.
#

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public — safe to expose. Sent to the browser.
# Row Level Security is what protects your data, not the secrecy of these keys.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Project Settings -> API -> Project URL
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=

# Project Settings -> API -> Project API keys -> anon / public
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secret — server-only. NEVER prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
#
# This key bypasses Row Level Security completely. Treat it like a database
# password: never commit it, never log it, never send it to the browser.
# Only lib/supabase/admin.js reads it, and that module is marked `server-only`
# so the build fails if it is ever imported into a Client Component.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Project Settings -> API -> Project API keys -> service_role
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional — canonical origin for links Supabase emails out (password resets).
#
# Leave blank and the origin is taken from the incoming request, which is
# correct for local development and preview deploys. Set it in production if
# the app sits behind a proxy that rewrites the Host header, or if reset links
# must always point at one canonical domain.
#
# No trailing slash. Example: https://knocknationbag.com
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional, secret — only for the schema scripts (npm run db:*). The app
# never reads it. Contains the database password: never commit it, never
# prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
#
# Dashboard -> Connect -> Session pooler. The direct db.<ref>.supabase.co host
# is IPv6-only and unreachable from many networks; the pooler works everywhere.
# Leave blank unless you are applying or checking migrations.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

SUPABASE_DB_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Razorpay — online payments. Test mode keys start with rzp_test_.
# Dashboard -> Settings -> API Keys (key id + secret) and
# Dashboard -> Webhooks (URL <site>/api/webhooks/razorpay; events payment.captured,
# order.paid, payment.failed, refund.processed; the secret you choose there).
# The key id is sent to the browser by the server; the two secrets never are.
# Leave empty and checkout offers Cash on Delivery only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=
RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
